.\" Manpage for localectl (localed bash client)
.TH LOCALECTL 1 "November 2026" "localed" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
localectl \- control the system locale and keyboard layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B localectl
.RB [ \-\-no\-pager ]
.IR COMMAND " [" ARGUMENT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B localectl
is a Bash client used to query and change the system locale and
keyboard layout configuration.
.PP
.B localectl
communicates with the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1
system D-Bus service to query and change locale and keyboard settings.
Configuration changes are sent to
.B localed
using the
.B SetLocale,
.B SetVConsoleKeyboard,
and
.B SetX11Keyboard
methods. The daemon validates and persists the settings, performs
PolKit authorization, and emits property-change signals.
.PP
Changing settings does not require running
.B localectl
as root when the calling user is authorized by the installed PolKit
policy. Otherwise, the D-Bus method may trigger an authentication prompt
when an agent is available. The
.B --no-convert
option disables conversion between console and X11 keyboard settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current locale and keyboard configuration in human-readable
form. This is the default command when none is given.
.TP
.BI list-keymaps " [FILTER]"
List all console keymaps installed under
.IR /usr/share/kbd/keymaps/ .
Keymap names are derived by stripping the directory path and
.B .map.gz
(or
.BR .map )
extension from each file found.
The optional
.I FILTER
argument is matched as a case-insensitive fixed string; regular-expression
metacharacters have no special meaning.
Does not require root.
.TP
.BI list-locales " [FILTER]"
List all locales available to the C library via
.BR "locale -a" .
The optional
.I FILTER
argument is matched as a case-insensitive fixed string; regular-expression
metacharacters have no special meaning. For example,
.B "localectl list-locales en_US"
narrows the output to en_US locales only.
Does not require root.
.TP
.BI set-locale " KEY=value [KEY=value ...]"
Set one or more locale variables.
.I KEY
must be one of
.BR LANG ,
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_CTYPE ,
.BR LC_NUMERIC ,
.BR LC_TIME ,
.BR LC_COLLATE ,
.BR LC_MONETARY ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
.BR LC_PAPER ,
.BR LC_NAME ,
.BR LC_ADDRESS ,
.BR LC_TELEPHONE ,
.BR LC_MEASUREMENT ,
or
.BR LC_IDENTIFICATION .
Each assignment is sent to the daemon over D-Bus and persisted using the Slackware locale configuration.
Passing an empty value (e.g.
.BR LC_TIME= )
removes that key from the file.
.TP
.BI set-keymap " KEYMAP [KEYMAP_TOGGLE]"
Set the virtual console keymap (and optionally the toggle keymap).
Sent to the daemon over D-Bus and persisted in the Slackware console-keymap configuration.
.TP
.BI set-x11-keymap " LAYOUT [MODEL [VARIANT [OPTIONS]]]"
Set the X11 keyboard layout.
.I LAYOUT
is required; all other arguments are optional.
Any argument not supplied is read from the current
.I X11_KEYBOARD_FILE
and preserved unchanged, so you can update a single field without
having to repeat all the others.
Pass an explicit empty string
.RB ( \(dq\(dq )
to clear a field.
Sent to the daemon over D-Bus and persisted in the X11 keyboard configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-convert
When used with
.B set-keymap
or
.BR set-x11-keymap ,
suppress the automatic conversion between the console keymap and the
X11 keyboard layout.
Without this flag,
.B set-keymap
also updates the X11 keyboard layout using the built-in conversion
table, and
.B set-x11-keymap
also updates the console keymap.
The conversion is best-effort; if no table entry exists for the given
keymap or layout, the other side is left unchanged rather than guessing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show the current status:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl status
.EE
.RE
.PP
List all available locales:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl list-locales
.EE
.RE
.PP
List only en_US locales:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl list-locales en_US
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the system locale:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl set-locale LANG=en_US.UTF-8
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set multiple locale variables at once:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl set-locale LANG=en_US.UTF-8 LC_TIME=en_GB.UTF-8
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the console keymap:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl set-keymap us
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the X11 keyboard layout with a variant:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl set-x11-keymap de pc105 nodeadkeys
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the X11 layout, model, variant, and compose key option:
.PP
.RS
.EX
localectl set-x11-keymap us pc105 "" compose:ralt
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI list-x11-keymap-models " [FILTER]"
List available X11 keyboard models from
.IR /usr/share/X11/xkb/rules/base.lst .
The optional
.I FILTER
is matched case-insensitively against the model code and description.
.TP
.BI list-x11-keymap-layouts " [FILTER]"
List available X11 keyboard layouts.
.TP
.BI "list-x11-keymap-variants [LAYOUT] [FILTER]"
List available X11 keyboard variants.
When
.I LAYOUT
is given, only variants that apply to that layout are printed
(matching the
.RI \(lq LAYOUT : \(rq
prefix in
.IR base.lst ).
.I FILTER
is applied on top of the layout restriction.
.TP
.BI list-x11-keymap-options " [FILTER]"
List available X11 keyboard options (e.g. compose key, Ctrl placement).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 1 on error (for example, an unknown locale
variable, an invalid value, a missing argument, or insufficient
permissions).
.SH AUTHORIZATION
The set commands communicate with
.B localed
through the system D-Bus and pass
.I interactive=true
so PolKit may display an authentication prompt when needed. Authorization
is determined by the daemon's PolKit policy and rules. The status command
also reads the D-Bus properties. The list commands only enumerate locally
installed data and do not require elevated privileges.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/lang.sh
Slackware locale shell script managed through the locale1 D-Bus service.
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/lang.csh
C-shell companion locale script updated alongside
.IR lang.sh .
.TP
.I /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap
Slackware console keyboard script. Regenerated atomically on every
.B set-keymap
invocation. The directory is created automatically if missing.
.TP
.I /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap.toggle
Sidecar file for the toggle keymap. Created when a toggle keymap is
set; removed when the toggle is cleared.
.TP
.I /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf
Xorg InputClass keyboard configuration managed by localed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR localed (8),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR gdbus (1),
.BR inotify (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Nathaniel Russell.
.PP
Part of the
.B localed
project, a non-systemd implementation of the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1
D-Bus interface for Slackware Linux.
